# Lifecycle verb: establish an MP_CAPABLE pair, then run the close/teardown race
# in one shot -- burst MP_JOIN SYNs at the still-open listener (each deferred to
# the NET_RX softirq) while synchronously closing the accepted server msk with
# SO_LINGER, racing the queued SYNs' softirq token lookups against the msk
# teardown. This is the close/join race class (finding 005's shape). On a fixed
# kernel it completes without crashing; if the race is won on a vulnerable kernel
# the kernel crashes -- that is the point of the verb.
#
# join_close_race is TERMINAL: it consumes the pair (frees the slot) itself, like
# pair_close -- so there is deliberately no pair_close after it.

r0 = syz_mptcp_pair_init(&AUTO={0x2, 0x0, @loopback}, &AUTO={0x2, 0x0, @loopback}, 0x0)
syz_mptcp_join_close_race(r0)
